'''Dwight Anderson''' (born July 5, 1981) is a Jamaican-born former professional [[gridiron football]] [[defensive back]] who played in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) and [[Canadian Football League]] (CFL). He was signed by the [[St. Louis Rams]] as an [[undrafted free agent]] in 2004.

Anderson was also a member of the NFL [[Carolina Panthers]], the [[Arena Football League|AFL]] team the [[Philadelphia Soul]], before becoming a [[Journeyman (sports)|journeyman]] across several [[Canadian Football League|CFL]] teams: the [[Hamilton Tiger-Cats]], [[Calgary Stampeders]], [[Montreal Alouettes]], [[Saskatchewan Roughriders]] and [[Toronto Argonauts]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Dwight Anderson Pro Football Record |url=https://www.profootballarchives.com/players/a/ande05250.html#gsc.tab=0 |access-date=2026-06-02 |website=www.profootballarchives.com}}</ref>

